    },
    {
      "id": "l4ieW58V7qqRQqD63hSWy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -435.4704509164968,
      "y": 423.1292384713863,
      "width": 537.7707099341615,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ae",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1748970258,
      "version": 616,
      "versionNonce": 1264983314,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792188550801,
      "created": 1792187959829,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Throughout the day, adenosine\naccumulates in the brain, binding to\nreceptors, which eventually leads to\ndrowsy feelings (aka increased 'sleep\npressure' over time).",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Throughout the day, adenosine accumulates in the brain, binding to receptors, which eventually leads to drowsy feelings (aka increased 'sleep pressure' over time).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hZLkDlAa0nIZROTfDtdGn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 32.51810666757615,
      "y": 394.5412762263242,
      "width": 7.3079986572265625,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "af",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2053098066,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1024991310,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792187996101,
      "created": 1792187994738,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FU4ti4f9n8pyO3L-fSBKG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -309.35041583620244,
      "y": 759.6649565245436,
      "width": 622.2775357809583,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ag",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 603370254,
      "version": 317,
      "versionNonce": 768169102,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792188503496,
      "created": 1792188093680,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Caffeine can bind to these specific receptors due\nto its shape. Since its not adenosine, it does not\nproduct the sleepy effect.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Caffeine can bind to these specific receptors due to its shape. Since its not adenosine, it does not product the sleepy effect.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_GgiSus3J_T_2hdlt4xXU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -395.18889081895117,
      "y": 979.1854763666882,
      "width": 793.9544847813345,
      "height": 218.90997186230882,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ah",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 421320018,
      "version": 1380,
      "versionNonce": 1382670546,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792188600321,
      "created": 1792188153763,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Once the caffeine is cleared out, adenosine can bind to the\nreceptors. Basically caffeine has a \"put off the sleepy\nfeelings until later\" mechanism.\n\nSleep is the only thing to effectively clear out adenosine.\nSort of why we have the whole \"I'm sleepy\" loop.",
      "fontSize": 29.187996248307844,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Once the caffeine is cleared out, adenosine can bind to the receptors. Basically caffeine has a \"put off the sleepy feelings until later\" mechanism.\n\nSleep is the only thing to effectively clear out adenosine. Sort of why we have the whole \"I'm sleepy\" loop.",
